module Core

### Represents the `Emittable` protocol.
### Iterators expose sequential access to values and advance their internal
### position each time `emit!` succeeds.
### :typeparam T: The element type yielded by the iterator.
protocol Emittable[T]
relates Item obeys Accessing[T]
    ### Returns the next value from this iterator.
    ### Implementations should return `absent` once the iterator is exhausted. What an iterator hands out is
    ### its `Item`, which reads as a `T`: a token on an element stored in a container (`Modifying[T]`, or
    ### `Viewing[T]` when the walk started from a read-only container), or the value itself when there is
    ### nothing stored to point at (a range, a generator). The builder takes `Item` from what `emit!`
    ### returns, so an iterator never names it.
    ### :returns: The next element in the iteration sequence.
    @writable
    routine Me.emit!() -> Me/Item
